  "rootAssessment": "Lead assent (Claude Opus 5.5) for inventory83 and the X3a-1 source boundary: law X3a r5. SelectedStoreEndpoint is validated in memory from the session's single read (pair, marker, the 64-node-bounded chain, the C.store join, the core closure and K), on the write side through OrdinaryWriteAdmission::admit_store_endpoint and on the read side through ReadSession::store_endpoint. Retained required files carry full metadata samples so that an in-place rewrite refuses; state.v1 is read once with its own cap and decoder. The creator path produces no endpoint. Grok r1 required the 64-node bound to give the budget row at G=63; r2 review.json reports ACCEPT-UNIT and inventoryCandidateAssessment ACCEPT, both with requiredFindings empty. I read both reviews. All source paths matched before commit. The real ~/Library/Application Support/OpenSIP is absent.",
